  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "EduUHJH+sLKVjHW36Gb3D3QueWg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:12.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The composition seam\n\nCodegen scaffolds a drive app as a `DriveExplorer` component, and the key detail is its props: it receives `children`, and `children` **is the mounted editor for the currently open document**. The drive app therefore decides where \u2014 and whether \u2014 the editor appears.\n\n```tsx\nexport function DriveExplorer({ children }: EditorProps) {\n  const showDocumentEditor = !!children;\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex h-full\">\n      <FolderTree />\n      <div className=\"flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-4\">\n        {showDocumentEditor ? children : <DriveContents />}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`!!children` is the whole selection test. When a document is open, `children` is truthy and the editor renders inside the drive app's layout. Otherwise the custom `DriveContents` fills the space \u2014 a Kanban board, a document grid, whatever the product needs.\n\n## Why children rather than a route swap\n\nPassing the editor as `children` means the drive app is not *replaced* when a document opens; it stays mounted and wraps the editor. That buys three things that a hard route switch does not:\n\n- **Persistent chrome.** A sidebar, breadcrumb, or filter panel keeps its state while the user moves between documents.\n- **Free choice of placement.** The editor can go in a main pane, a split view, a slide-over panel, or a modal \u2014 the drive app owns the layout decision, not Connect.\n- **The option to ignore it.** A drive app that never renders `children` simply never shows the editor, which is a legitimate design for a read-only dashboard.\n\nThe trade is that forgetting to render `children` produces a drive app where opening a document appears to do nothing. There is no error \u2014 the editor mounted correctly and was handed to a parent that dropped it.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/05-connect/02-drive-apps.mdx (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:12.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:12.000Z"
    }
  },
